    24	 * With no such rate the due is not fixed. The user who opened the claim, or last edited it, may not settle it.
    25	 * When a clerk (any user not made a steward) settles a claim whose due is above the sheet's clerk
    26	 * limit, it goes to PENDING instead, its due left live until a steward approves or rejects it; a
    27	 * due of n/a is within any limit. Before the clerk limit is considered, a claim whose due is above
    28	 * the proof threshold in force on its date is refused while it has no proofs, or none of a kind the proof kinds list. Only a role the
    29	 * permission matrix allows may settle.
    30	 * <p>
    31	 * Settled as of a date (on or before the sheet's today), the due fixed is the claim's due as it stood
    32	 * at the end of that date ({@link #dueAsOf}); a date after today, or one before the claim was added,
