    38	 * Adds and opens a claim per pasted line, in order, for the person on the sheet with that name (matched
    39	 * as names are compared). A line naming the date and note of one of its person's claims as they stood
    40	 * before the paste (not VOID nor DELETED, nor taken by an earlier line) updates that claim instead: the
    41	 * newest such DRAFT is edited to the line's amount and opened; a line whose matches hold no DRAFT is
    42	 * refused. Every line is checked first, as the claim form checks a claim (its person on the sheet, its
    43	 * reference unused on the sheet and in the paste, its due-by outside a closed period and not after its
    44	 * person's retirement) and as the editor checks an edit (not locked by another user, its lines' total), and its person under the sheet's maximum of open claims,
    45	 * then each is opened as the open button opens it (the user's role allowed to open, a note when its due
    46	 * needs one, its period's cap). One refusal refuses the whole paste: it is a single transaction, and
    47	 * its audit lines are only written once every line has gone through. Each line writes CLAIM_ADDED (or
    48	 * CLAIM_EDITED when its amount changed), then CLAIM_OPENED, then the figures it moved.
